  "id": "Compound::DB06770 - Gene::1555",
  "verbalization": "Benzyl Alcohol is shown to bind to Cyp2d6, a gene that is involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. This binding is supported by two distinct paths, both of which indicate that Cyp2d6 participates in the epoxygenation and monooxygenation of arachidonic acid, activities that are catalyzed by Cyp2b6. The shared pathway suggests a potential functional link between Benzyl Alcohol and Cyp2b6, as the drug may influence the activity of Cyp2d6, which in turn affects the metabolism of arachidonic acid. The presence of a common intermediate, arachidonic acid, indicates that the drug may modulate the expression or activity of Cyp2b6 through a mechanism involving the enzyme Cyp2d6. The evidence is consistent and supports a mechanistic relationship between Benzyl Alcohol and Cyp2b6, particularly through the involvement of Cyp2d6 in the metabolic pathway of arachidonic acid.",
